#!/usr/bin/env ssc
---
name: derives-schema
exports:
  - Labelled
  - LabelledInstance
---

# A `derives`-able typeclass in ANOTHER module

Exists so `js-derives-segmented` can pin the IMPORTED-typeclass scan path, which is a
different code path from a typeclass declared in the importing module.

```scalascript
trait Labelled[A]:
  def label(): String

case class LabelledInstance(text: String) extends Labelled[Any]:
  def label(): String = text

object Labelled:
  def derived(m: Mirror): Labelled[Any] =
    LabelledInstance(m.label + "/" + m.elemLabels.length.toString)
```
